 lot of success with people  reporting human trafficking in their  communities since then  mrs. pence I want to ask you as a former  educator about just some things that  we're seeing in the news today obviously  school safety is a huge issue  there are going to be a number of  students from parkland who are heading  to Washington on Saturday for a March  and I wonder what your thoughts are on  that well you know honestly I feel like  as as second lady that no one elected me  or voted for me and so I hesitate to  talk policy just because I feel like  people would think well who does she  think she is telling us what she thinks  policy should be I mean we definitely  discuss a lot of these issues at home  but I mean we all want our schools to be  safe and so I'm also along with all the  other Americans looking to our elected  officials to say we need to do something  to keep our children safe in school  that's in one place they should be safe  Charlotte do you have any thoughts on  that  these young people coming from parkland  from other schools as well that are  planning to come and just express their  thoughts on this any you have any kind  of feeling about that to see young  people coming to the nation's capital E  yeah I think it's just what my mom said  honestly I mean I think everyone wants  to you know see this violence stop and a  light I mean like I said before I mean  that's what freedom looks like and I  think it's I think it's it's great for  anybody to voice their opinions and to  you know take advantage of our rights to  gather and and to protest to speak out  what surprised you about being in  Washington so far is there anything that  you can think of off the top of your  head was it what you thought it would be  was it perhaps not all you thought it  would be I don't know I think I think  about it it's kind of funny since we're  still in it I think we'll look back on  things and I'll be able to tell you that  what surprised me or not but our family  